1
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:05,881
Ah, a mother's set.

2
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:08,675
It's the sigil of the artist
who made it,

3
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,552
a unique signature.

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,596
Don't try to stop us...

5
00:00:15,516 --> 00:00:18,101
Ellora's mine
to protect because...

6
00:00:18,227 --> 00:00:20,270
I'm the Avatar!

7
00:00:20,729 --> 00:00:22,105
<i>She's your ward.</i>

8
00:00:22,648 --> 00:00:24,775
<i>You hid her true nature
from me!</i>

9
00:00:26,485 --> 00:00:28,278
Run, Nisha!

10
00:00:30,906 --> 00:00:31,990
Ow!

11
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:34,868
Commander Karthik,
you are under arrest!

12
00:00:35,661 --> 00:00:38,205
<i>Where did
the Avatar go, traitor?</i>

13
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:40,122
<i>No idea...</i>

14
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:41,875
<i>but you won't find her.</i>

15
00:00:44,795 --> 00:00:46,213
<i>Fire.</i>

16
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:48,005
<i>Air.</i>

17
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:49,091
<i>Water.</i>

18
00:00:49,675 --> 00:00:50,634
<i>Earth.</i>

19
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:54,096
<i>Long ago, the Avatar,</i>

20
00:00:54,221 --> 00:00:56,265
<i>master of all four elements,</i>

21
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:58,559
<i>brought forth the Cataclysm.</i>

22
00:00:58,934 --> 00:01:00,393
<i>Out of the devastation,</i>

23
00:01:00,394 --> 00:01:03,312
<i>the world built
the Seven Havens.</i>

24
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:05,315
<i>Now the Avatar has returned,</i>

25
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:08,277
<i>but for the first time,
there are two.</i>

26
00:01:08,777 --> 00:01:11,320
<i>Most fear they'll destroy
the world again...</i>

27
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:12,948
<i>But I believe...</i>

28
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:14,365
<i>they will save it.</i>

29
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:22,790
There she is!

30
00:01:22,791 --> 00:01:24,126
Down with the Avatar!

31
00:01:24,251 --> 00:01:27,461
- Let's teach her a lesson!
- Hurry, before she gets away!

32
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:30,632
Leave me alone!

33
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:47,524
Geet...

34
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:51,028
Another nightmare.

35
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:53,447
Nisha...

36
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:56,074
Where are you?

37
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:05,292
<i>Elloran citizens,</i>

38
00:02:05,709 --> 00:02:07,753
<i>the Council asks
for your cooperation</i>

39
00:02:07,878 --> 00:02:10,339
<i>as we continue our hunt
for the Avatar.</i>

40
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:12,131
<i>Stay in your homes,</i>

41
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:15,676
<i>report any suspicious behavior
to the authorities.</i>

42
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:21,892
Sang! It's good
to see you again!

43
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:23,976
Get back! No passage!

44
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:25,687
Please, my mother is sick!

45
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:27,189
No movement
between districts

46
00:02:27,314 --> 00:02:28,648
without travel documents

47
00:02:28,649 --> 00:02:30,400
by order of the Chancellor!

48
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:44,747
It's been two weeks.

49
00:02:44,748 --> 00:02:47,501
Surely the Avatar
couldn't have vanished.

50
00:02:47,626 --> 00:02:49,752
I have the
entire Brigade looking,

51
00:02:49,753 --> 00:02:51,171
but so far
there's no trace of her.

52
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:53,382
Someone must be helping her.

53
00:02:53,757 --> 00:02:55,675
You put Karthik
and the White Lotus

54
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:57,134
in prison yourself.

55
00:02:57,135 --> 00:02:59,221
There's no way
they've contacted Nisha.

56
00:02:59,346 --> 00:03:01,430
What about
the Avatar's twin sister?

57
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:03,475
What twin sister?

58
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,017
She...

59
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:07,311
...is just a simple earthbender.

60
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:08,396
I didn't think she was of any--

61
00:03:08,397 --> 00:03:10,857
I don't care
about her abilities!

62
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:13,025
She might have information!

63
00:03:13,026 --> 00:03:14,986
Why aren't we looking for her?

64
00:03:15,362 --> 00:03:17,154
What else
haven't you told me, Jae?

65
00:03:17,155 --> 00:03:19,032
Are you still
in Karthik's pocket?

66
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:21,117
Chancellor Kayoko,

67
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:24,204
you have my word
that I am Ellora's servant,

68
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:25,496
always.

69
00:03:25,497 --> 00:03:26,997
Lan, I'm putting you in charge

70
00:03:26,998 --> 00:03:28,792
of finding the Avatar's sister.

71
00:03:29,835 --> 00:03:31,545
Let's not take any chances.

72
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:33,922
We will also offer
a sizable reward

73
00:03:34,047 --> 00:03:36,090
to anyone
who can bring us the girl.

74
00:03:36,091 --> 00:03:37,217
Yes, Chancellor.

75
00:03:37,801 --> 00:03:40,137
At least we won't have
to make new posters!

76
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:43,431
Because they're twins?

77
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:53,232
Lan, when you find Pavi,

78
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,026
bring her straight to me.

79
00:03:55,152 --> 00:03:56,069
Understood?

80
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:58,363
You got it, um, Commander!

81
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:01,074
Sorry, that's still
weird to say.

82
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:02,284
Tell me about it.

83
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:07,037
Hmm.

84
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:23,972
Ah!

85
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:32,229
Oh, no, you don't.

86
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:33,856
My cat-monkey is not your lunch!

87
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:39,821
Why don't you buzz off!

88
00:04:42,783 --> 00:04:44,284
Ha!

89
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:46,620
That's why you don't mess
with the Avatar!

90
00:04:50,874 --> 00:04:53,292
What does being the Avatar
even mean anymore?

91
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:01,218
Come on, Ruhi.
Let's get back to shelter.

92
00:05:19,069 --> 00:05:20,862
I know, Sang.

93
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:22,072
What a mess.

94
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:23,782
Sorry I'm late.

95
00:05:24,241 --> 00:05:27,117
It's getting harder and harder
to scrounge up a decent snack!

96
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:29,411
Did you learn
anything new this week?

97
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:31,081
Do you know
where my sister went?

98
00:05:32,082 --> 00:05:34,793
Actually, I finally found
something out.

99
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:36,418
Something big.

100
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:37,753
Really?

101
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:38,672
What is it? I--

102
00:05:38,797 --> 00:05:40,131
It'll cost you the usual,

103
00:05:40,257 --> 00:05:42,008
three bao and an apple.

104
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:43,969
I don't have that.

105
00:05:44,094 --> 00:05:45,344
Make up your mind, kid.

106
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:48,265
Either cough up something
to trade, or I walk.

107
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:52,394
Hmm.

108
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:58,733
Wait, wasn't this your mom's?

109
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:01,444
It's all I have left.

110
00:06:01,945 --> 00:06:03,654
If it gets me to Nisha,

111
00:06:03,655 --> 00:06:04,781
then it's worth it.

112
00:06:05,657 --> 00:06:07,033
So what did you find out?

113
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:10,036
Is Nisha close?
Can I go see her?

114
00:06:12,122 --> 00:06:14,791
This place isn't safe.
Follow me.

115
00:06:16,585 --> 00:06:18,670
- We gotta find her.
- I'll take the right.

116
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:21,046
So what did you learn?

117
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:22,632
Nothing about Nisha,

118
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:25,759
but I did learn that the Council
put out a big reward

119
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,554
for the Avatar's sister.

120
00:06:29,598 --> 00:06:30,973
How could you?

121
00:06:30,974 --> 00:06:32,308
Easy. They're paying me.

122
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:34,435
Listen to me, Pavi,
I can explain.

123
00:06:34,436 --> 00:06:35,770
Explain what?

124
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:37,647
I know what you did, traitor!

125
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:42,484
Mr. Beetle, please,

126
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:43,986
I don't want to smash you!

127
00:06:45,196 --> 00:06:46,448
Take it easy.

128
00:06:46,573 --> 00:06:48,116
Not a chance!

129
00:06:50,744 --> 00:06:51,952
Pavi, wait!

130
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:56,832
- Should we pursue, Commander?
- No.

131
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:58,793
Let her go.

132
00:06:58,919 --> 00:07:01,670
All right. I'll knock
10 percent off the reward.

133
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:03,632
But that's my final offer.

134
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:06,801
Fifteen percent?

135
00:07:07,719 --> 00:07:09,054
Okay, 20!

136
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:12,766
Now everyone's
looking for me too!

137
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:14,351
What are we gonna do?

138
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:22,150
Nisha, what would you do?

139
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:32,535
I can't find my sister, but...

140
00:07:33,203 --> 00:07:37,165
do you think maybe
we can finally find Mom and Dad?

141
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:07,486
Sorry, Ruhi.

142
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:10,073
You really are more
of an indoor cat-monkey.

143
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:14,202
Pavi...

144
00:08:14,703 --> 00:08:15,912
where are you?

145
00:08:19,082 --> 00:08:21,333
<i>Nisha...</i>

146
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:22,544
Did you hear that,

147
00:08:23,128 --> 00:08:25,296
or am I getting sand sickness?

148
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:26,798
Wait...

149
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:29,425
Didn't Jae say something
about connecting

150
00:08:29,426 --> 00:08:31,636
with all sorts of things
when your mind is quiet?

151
00:08:32,511 --> 00:08:35,515
Maybe he was onto something
with that meditation stuff.

152
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:43,355
Okay. My mind is clear.

153
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:45,483
I'm focused on the energy
around me.

154
00:08:46,026 --> 00:08:49,446
Just... be... still.

155
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:02,709
Pavi...

156
00:09:09,299 --> 00:09:10,258
Ruhi...

157
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:12,927
It's just a little thunder.

158
00:09:27,776 --> 00:09:28,610
You wanna piece of me?

159
00:09:28,735 --> 00:09:30,236
Come on! I've already taken down

160
00:09:30,361 --> 00:09:32,238
one overgrown bully today!

161
00:09:34,991 --> 00:09:35,825
Huh?

162
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:37,994
Why are you just staring
at me like that?

163
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:39,788
Show me what you got!

164
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:46,086
Wait. How'd you get
in here, anyway?

165
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:57,514
You're not from this world.

166
00:09:58,306 --> 00:09:59,808
You're a spirit!

167
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:01,309
Wow...

168
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:03,019
What do you want?

169
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:04,437
Wait.

170
00:10:04,813 --> 00:10:05,979
Do spirits want things?

171
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,236
Hey, where are you going?

172
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:22,705
Wait for us!

173
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:30,046
I guess we lived
pretty far out in the dunes.

174
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,884
That's the Bristlethorn!

175
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,220
Come on, Geet!

176
00:10:48,982 --> 00:10:51,276
There's nothing here.

177
00:10:52,986 --> 00:10:54,779
Just like Karthik said.

178
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:57,239
Huh?

179
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:04,414
Wait.

180
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:17,802
There's something here.

181
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:30,190
Geet...

182
00:11:31,399 --> 00:11:32,609
we're home.

183
00:11:35,111 --> 00:11:37,487
Why haven't
they found the Avatar?

184
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:39,448
She must be hiding somewhere.

185
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:42,534
Ugh! Maybe she's gone
to another haven?

186
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:44,454
Let me go or I'll bite!

187
00:11:44,913 --> 00:11:46,663
Listen here,
you little urchin!

188
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:49,374
My apologies, Chancellor.

189
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:51,668
I demand payment for finding

190
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:53,004
the Avatar's sister!

191
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:56,090
You found her?

192
00:11:56,216 --> 00:11:57,258
Does the Avatar's twin

193
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:59,052
have the power of invisibility?

194
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:02,304
I practically had her
gift wrapped for you.

195
00:12:02,305 --> 00:12:04,891
It's not my fault
your benders bungled it!

196
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:07,894
The reward
is for capturing the twin.

197
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:09,771
Not pointing her out.

198
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:13,608
Then how about I give you
a second crack at her?

199
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:14,776
For a price.

200
00:12:14,901 --> 00:12:16,611
You know where she is?

201
00:12:17,237 --> 00:12:18,196
Maybe.

202
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:21,323
How does a month's worth

203
00:12:21,324 --> 00:12:22,909
of rations sound?

204
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:24,034
You've got a deal!

205
00:12:24,035 --> 00:12:25,286
I bumped into Pavi

206
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:26,996
a couple of weeks ago.

207
00:12:27,622 --> 00:12:29,456
She was... uh...

208
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:30,959
robbing a local jeweler.

209
00:12:31,334 --> 00:12:32,585
Bad egg, that one.

210
00:12:33,211 --> 00:12:35,170
She's been looking
for her parents

211
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:37,756
in the Eastern Outskirts.

212
00:13:22,302 --> 00:13:23,177
Dad.

213
00:13:30,101 --> 00:13:31,810
Mom.

214
00:13:31,811 --> 00:13:34,397
Found you! I told you
I'm the best at hiding!

215
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:37,274
No fair!

216
00:13:37,275 --> 00:13:39,694
You know I can't airbend
as good as you!

217
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:42,071
I'll help you!

218
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:53,415
Got you!

219
00:13:55,209 --> 00:13:56,544
Jump! Come on!

220
00:14:00,298 --> 00:14:01,507
Let's go!

221
00:14:05,053 --> 00:14:07,263
All right, you two
know the rules.

222
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:08,847
No bending in the house.

223
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:11,308
Come on, those eggplants
won't pick themselves.

224
00:14:11,309 --> 00:14:13,686
- Aw!
- Aw, chores!

225
00:14:14,062 --> 00:14:15,187
Let's all go!

226
00:14:15,188 --> 00:14:17,731
I bet the raspberries
are nice and ripe too!

227
00:14:17,732 --> 00:14:18,607
No...

228
00:14:18,608 --> 00:14:19,942
No, come back!

229
00:14:27,742 --> 00:14:29,577
So much of that searching,

230
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:31,913
and Nisha was right.

231
00:14:32,497 --> 00:14:34,749
There's nothing here
but ghosts...

232
00:14:40,088 --> 00:14:42,965
Nisha... where are you?

233
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:48,512
Ruhi, I'm the bridge

234
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:50,889
between the physical
and spirit worlds, right?

235
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,016
Maybe when I was trying
to reach Pavi,

236
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:54,726
I called this spirit instead?

237
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:59,065
That looks like a big one.

238
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:01,359
Uh, excuse me,

239
00:15:01,484 --> 00:15:04,194
O great... Spirit Beast,

240
00:15:04,195 --> 00:15:05,947
but I think we need
to find shelter

241
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:07,490
before that storm hits.

242
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:11,494
Where are we going, anyway?

243
00:15:13,079 --> 00:15:16,290
Oh, no, no!
I can't go back to Ellora!

244
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:18,084
Everyone hates me there.

245
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:20,752
Hello? Did you hear me?

246
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:22,380
Avatar no welcome!

247
00:15:22,505 --> 00:15:25,007
Humans want to destroy me
for all time!

248
00:15:29,846 --> 00:15:31,931
Wait. That looks familiar.

249
00:15:32,682 --> 00:15:34,475
I've seen this place.

250
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:36,519
Why did you bring me here?

251
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:40,523
Wait! Where are you going?

252
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,541
It's okay, Ruhi.

253
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:21,522
Wait!

254
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:22,898
Mom! Dad!

255
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:32,575
No!

256
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:38,080
No...

257
00:16:38,206 --> 00:16:40,541
It... It can't be true.

258
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:46,380
Nisha!

259
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:51,385
Come on!

260
00:17:11,906 --> 00:17:13,907
Nisha!

261
00:17:15,867 --> 00:17:16,953
Pavi?

262
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:30,966
I'm so sorry, Nisha.

263
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:34,762
Wherever our parents are,
I'm done chasing the past.

264
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:38,766
From now on, the only thing
I care about is you and me.

265
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:41,185
Do you forgive me?

266
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:47,275
Sisters always forgive
one another, right?

267
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,158
Are you okay?

268
00:17:57,159 --> 00:17:57,994
What happened?

269
00:17:58,119 --> 00:18:00,537
I felt you were in pain,

270
00:18:00,538 --> 00:18:02,915
right here in my heart.

271
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:06,127
Uh...

272
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:08,004
I...

273
00:18:12,967 --> 00:18:14,594
I saw a spirit!

274
00:18:14,719 --> 00:18:17,054
And-and it, uh...

275
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:18,431
a-attacked me!

276
00:18:18,848 --> 00:18:20,432
I barely got out alive.

277
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:25,395
Don't worry. From now on,

278
00:18:25,396 --> 00:18:28,232
we tackle
mean old spirits together!

279
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:29,525
Twin promise!

280
00:18:34,322 --> 00:18:35,363
Uh...

281
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:37,950
what about giant sandstorms?

282
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:41,037
We gotta find more shelter!

283
00:18:48,502 --> 00:18:49,669
What do we do?

284
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:50,838
I don't know!

285
00:18:53,633 --> 00:18:55,259
Uh, Pavi...

286
00:18:55,676 --> 00:18:57,135
A-Are you doing this?

287
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:58,471
Definitely not me.

288
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:00,598
Nisha!

289
00:19:00,723 --> 00:19:02,098
I can't see!

290
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:03,476
Oh, sorry!

291
00:19:03,601 --> 00:19:04,726
I'm here!

292
00:19:04,727 --> 00:19:06,228
Ruhi!

293
00:19:06,354 --> 00:19:07,688
Yeah. I know it's dark.

294
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:10,566
Did the desert just...

295
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:11,942
swallow us?

296
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:13,986
Not exactly.

297
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:15,445
You!

298
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:17,406
Why, hello again, young Avatar!

299
00:19:17,907 --> 00:19:19,825
It looked like
you could use a little help.

300
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:22,327
Why would we ever
trust you again?

301
00:19:22,328 --> 00:19:25,206
Because unlike
most of the people

302
00:19:25,331 --> 00:19:26,581
in your life right now,

303
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:29,918
I am actually in a position
to help you.

304
00:19:43,307 --> 00:19:44,642
Oh.

305
00:19:44,767 --> 00:19:47,436
Move aside.
I need to access the prison.

306
00:19:48,771 --> 00:19:50,815
As you wish, Commander!

307
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:55,236
Thank you!

308
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:56,821
I mean, that's right.

309
00:19:56,946 --> 00:19:58,322
I <i>am</i> the Commander.

310
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:03,743
Hello? Shilpa? Daemin?

311
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:04,787
It's Jae...

312
00:20:05,413 --> 00:20:06,414
Jae?

313
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:08,040
What are you doing down here?

314
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:10,042
Datu! Uh...

315
00:20:10,167 --> 00:20:12,253
I was just coming to interrogate
the White Lotus

316
00:20:12,378 --> 00:20:13,545
about the Avatar's whereabouts.

317
00:20:13,546 --> 00:20:15,548
What about you?
How's your day been?

318
00:20:15,673 --> 00:20:17,674
The Chancellor
moved those traitors

319
00:20:17,675 --> 00:20:18,801
to a new facility.

320
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:20,886
She's worried someone might try
to break them out.

321
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:23,347
Ah! Good thinking!

322
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:26,559
Our Chancellor
is always one step ahead!

323
00:20:28,102 --> 00:20:30,771
You wouldn't by any chance know
where that new facility is,

324
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:32,481
would you... sweetie?

325
00:20:32,982 --> 00:20:35,943
I've been ordered not to reveal
their whereabouts.

326
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:38,027
Hey, look.

327
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:39,822
I know why you didn't tell me

328
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:41,365
about the White Lotus.

329
00:20:42,116 --> 00:20:44,410
Just like I didn't tell you
about Molin.

330
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:49,330
How about we vow, from now on,
to be honest with each other.

331
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:51,041
No more secrets?

332
00:20:53,294 --> 00:20:55,504
I'm sorry I've hidden
so much from you.

333
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:59,508
I'm just so glad
we're on the same page now.

334
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:07,600
Ugh!

335
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:11,019
Wait. I thought we were
going someplace safe!

336
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:12,979
My creepy cave
is better than this.

337
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:14,732
Looks can be deceiving.

338
00:21:14,857 --> 00:21:17,650
Is that so,
friendly neighborhood cook?

339
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:19,445
Ooh-hoo-hoo! Nice one!

340
00:21:29,038 --> 00:21:30,706
Whoa!

341
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:40,174
The Avatar <i>and</i> the Faceless?

342
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:43,343
The Chancellor is gonna love us.

343
00:21:43,344 --> 00:21:44,637
Yeah, she will!

344
00:21:44,762 --> 00:21:46,638
That sizable reward is ours!

345
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:48,390
Shh!

